{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUAMs5qNGnM98y8KXdJJdG","type":"tool_result","content":"4898-\n4899-@mcp.tool()\n4900:def submit_dream_review_report(\n4901-    report: str,\n4902-    project: str,\n4903-    tier: str,\n4904-    dream_id: str,\n4905-    overall_score: str = \"\",\n4906-    review_chat_id: str = \"\",\n4907-    review_visible: bool = True,\n4908-) -> str:\n4909-    \"\"\"Deliver a Dream-mode review report (Dream Review Director only).\n4910-\n4911-    Persists the review to ``dream_reports/{dream_id}/{tier}/review_report.md``\n4912-    and (optionally) posts a Group C visibility card. The Dream Tool reads\n4913-    the file once your subprocess exits — there is NO Research Director\n4914-    delivery, NO ``review_reports/round_N.md``, NO ``review_issues.yaml``,\n4915-    and NO 5-step protocol attached.\n4916-\n4917-    Use this in place of ``submit_review_report_to_research_director`` for\n4918-    Dream-mode roundtable Step 4. See DREAM_AGENT_DESIGN.md §6.4.\n4919-\n4920-    Args:\n4921-        report: Consolidated review report text (covers all Dream reviewers).\n4922-        project: Current project name.\n4923-        tier: Which Dream tier this report covers — ``best`` / ``median``\n4924-            / ``worst``.\n4925-        dream_id: Dream invocation id (with or without the ``dream_`` prefix —\n4926-            both accepted).\n4927-        overall_score: Optional headline assessment (\"strong reject\",\n4928-            \"borderline accept\", etc.).\n4929-        review_chat_id: Group C chat_id (loaded from project config when empty).\n4930-        review_visible: When True (default) posts a visibility card to Group C\n4931-            with a ``[Dream]`` prefix. Set False for silent submission.\n4932-    \"\"\"\n4933:    result = feishu_group_mod.submit_dream_review_report(\n4934-        report=report,\n4935-        project=project,\n4936-        tier=tier,\n4937-        dream_id=dream_id,\n4938-        overall_score=overall_score,\n4939-        review_chat_id=review_chat_id,\n4940-        review_visible=review_visible,\n4941-    )\n4942-    return _tool_result_to_str(result)\n4943-\n4944-\n4945-@mcp.tool()\n4946-def request_external_review(\n4947-    project: str,\n4948-    paper_pdf_path: str,\n4949-    venue: str = \"\",\n4950-    note: str = \"\",\n4951-    chat_id: str = \"\",\n4952-    reminder_hours: int = 8,\n4953-) -> str:\n4954-    \"\"\"Request human-assisted external review via Stanford Agentic Reviewer (paperreview.ai).\n4955-\n4956-    Sends an interactive card to the user group (Group A) with instructions\n4957-    to manually submit the paper PDF on paperreview.ai.  A reminder is\n4958-    automatically scheduled after ``reminder_hours`` to follow up.\n4959-\n4960-    The user will paste the external review text back into the chat when\n4961-    it arrives.  This tool does NOT block — internal review should proceed\n4962-    in parallel.\n4963-\n4964-    Args:\n4965-        project: Current project name.\n4966-        paper_pdf_path: Path to the paper PDF on the server.\n4967-        venue: Target venue (e.g. \"EMNLP 2026\") — helps user select on paperreview.ai.\n4968-        note: Optional note for the user.\n4969-        chat_id: Group A chat_id (optional, loads from project config).\n4970-        reminder_hours: Hours before auto-reminder (default 8).\n4971-    \"\"\"\n4972-    result = external_review_mod.request_external_review(\n4973-        project=project,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40c7584a-1cbd-47aa-9ea9-858c21cd14fb","uuid":"f152df17-f17c-4cce-8664-5cc9975c3753","timestamp":"2026-05-12T02:57:24.470Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"4898-\n4899-@mcp.tool()\n4900:def submit_dream_review_report(\n4901-    report: str,\n4902-    project: str,\n4903-    tier: str,\n4904-    dream_id: str,\n4905-    overall_score: str = \"\",\n4906-    review_chat_id: str = \"\",\n4907-    review_